From: Harris Hancock <harris@cloudflare.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:31:26 +0100
Subject: Allow V8 release archives without metagen Clang headers

workerd builds V8 from GitHub source archives, which do not include the
Clang files downloaded by gclient. V8 requires the optional metagen
header glob to match while loading the Bazel package even though metagen
is disabled, so the archive cannot otherwise be built.

Allow the glob to be empty. Builds that enable metagen still require the
actual Clang headers.

Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6-sol

diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
index c75adb604ede34589eaee4cc108133c75044823d..e40bb6e41247a538e7949a34c60cc5a2aa4ddd1d 100644
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -4588,7 +4588,7 @@ filegroup(
     name = "metagen_clang_builtin_headers",
     srcs = glob([
         "third_party/llvm-build/Release+Asserts/lib/clang/*/include/**",
-    ]),
+    ], allow_empty = True),
 )
 
